   ButtonNote->"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tachyonic_antitelephone"],
  Annotation[#, "http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tachyonic_antitelephone", 
   "Hyperlink"]& ]], "Output",
 CellChangeTimes->{3.468690232880711*^9},
 FontSize->16]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[TextData[{
 "One can imagine a world so deterministic that Alice/Bob are prevented from \
making the choices that would expose results inconsistent with determinism. \
Conway & Kochen dismiss this possibility on grounds that ",
 StyleBox["in such a conspiratorial world (where the free decisions of \
experimentalists are constrained) science is impossible",
  FontVariations->{"Underline"->True}],
 ".\n"
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.468629393658593*^9, 3.4686295330381193`*^9}, 
   3.468629634294273*^9, {3.468629684035624*^9, 3.46862987213941*^9}, 
   3.468713390608848*^9},
 FontSize->18],

Cell[TextData[{
 "\nSince about 1990, Gerard 't Hooft has been cultivating a theory which \
purports to deduce quantum theory from ",
 StyleBox["a completely deterministic physics at the Planck scale",
  FontVariations->{"Underline"->True}],
 ". He claims that the Conway/Kochen argument fails because Alice/Bob \
actually do NOT have free will they imagine themselves to have\[Ellipsis]so \
therefore neither do particles."
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.46862990967795*^9, 3.468630167129558*^9}, {
   3.468630201760935*^9, 3.4686302238072166`*^9}, {3.4686896532618513`*^9, 
   3.468689658101774*^9}, 3.468710430333459*^9},
 FontSize->18],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Hyperlink", "[", 
  RowBox[{
  "\"\<Determinism Beneath Quantum Mechanics\>\"", ",", 
   "\"\<http://arxiv.org/pdf/quant-ph/0212095v1\>\""}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.468689318195628*^9, 3.4686893700069113`*^9}},
 FontSize->16],

